---
<p>Bayan reads a little like Python with the types written in: short lines, no ceremony, a <code>for</code> loop over anything. The differences are underneath. Types are checked before the program runs, integers have a size, values are copied or moved on purpose, and a function that can fail says so in its signature. This guide maps what you do in Python to what you write in Bayan, then explains the parts that will surprise you.</p>
<p>Every Bayan program on this page was run with the compiler, and the output shown is its real output.</p>

